; ─── THE MARKET YARD ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; Built to test ONE thing: does money mean more when there is somewhere to spend
; it before the exit? So the arithmetic is the content, and it is deliberate.
;
;   safe plaza coins     16 x 5  =  80
;   coins among thieves  10 x 5  =  50
;   TOTAL ON THE FLOOR           = 130
;   exit                         = 110
;   priced gate                  =  30, and a 70 chest behind it
;   garlic                       =  10 each, five in stock
;
; Which makes three real plays rather than one:
;
;   HOARD      130 covers the 110 exit with 20 to spare. Tight: lose two hits
;              worth of money to a thief you fail to catch and you cannot leave
;              until you kill it.
;   INVEST     pay 30 for the gate and you are down to 100 with an exit that
;              wants 110 — the scary part is not the 30, it is walking around
;              underfunded — then the chest pays 70 and you leave with 60 spare.
;   SURVIVE    garlic at 10 competes directly with both of the above.
;
; The gate guards an OPTIONAL chest, never the exit. A gate on the critical path
; is a toll, not a decision.
